  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM &#x2013; Multi Country Humanitarian Assistance &#x2013; CAP 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite the state of siege declared by the Congolese authorities since 6 May 2021 to track down and neutralize armed groups in North Kivu and Ituri provinces, insecurity continues to spread in these parts of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) leading to violence and massacres of civilians, human rights violations, and massive displacement of populations. In all affected areas, humanitarian needs include lack of access to basic services, essential household items, shelter, and healthcare. The protection of populations, particularly their dignity, physical and psychological integrity is one of the major humanitarian challenges. Interventions planned under this project directly contribute to improving the living conditions of the conflict-affected populations including internally displaced persons and host communities in by providing lifesaving humanitarian assistance in spontaneous displacement sites and surrounding communities in Ituri, North Kivu, and Tanganyika provinces, while also providing evidence on mental health and psychosocial support needs assistance for conflict-affected populations in Eastern DRC.</narrative>
  </description>
